 to address the following problem: finding the unique solution to the initial value problem
$$
\begin{aligned}
\begin{cases}
\frac{d}{dt} u(t) + A(u(t)) = 0, & t > 0, \\
u(0) = u_0,
\end{cases}
\end{aligned}
$$
where the nonlinear, possibly unbounded operator $A$ is defined on a Hilbert space $\mathcal{H}$. The scheme is constructed by combining the implicit midpoint rule with the Fréchet–Nevanlinna–Nevanlinna (FNN) method. Under the assumption that the operator $A$ is maximal monotone, the scheme is proven to be stable and accurate. Furthermore, the paper demonstrates that the scheme converges to the unique solution of the initial value problem. The approach is also applied to the Navier–Stokes–Cauchy problem.

